cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its output tables, cite it as below."
title: "EBNA1-MimicScan"
abstract: >-
  A reproducibility-first screen for human proteins that the immune system could
  mistake for EBNA1. Two deliberately separate channels: an anchored screen
  starting from the antibody-validated EBNA1 386-440 epitope region, and an
  unbiased screen of all 641 EBNA1 residues against 20,431 reviewed human
  proteins. Every candidate is calibrated against same-composition shuffles, and
  every candidate-ranking axis is first validated against the published mimics it
  is supposed to recover.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shiningleeeee/EBNA1-MimicScan"
keywords:
  - molecular mimicry
  - Epstein-Barr virus
  - EBNA1
  - multiple sclerosis
  - composition-controlled null model
  - reproducibility
